1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Most people blame heavy periods and pelvic pressure on stress or genetics.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,480
Research points to something else instead.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,280
Fibroids are non-cancerous growths that respond to estrogen and progesterone.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,880
They're incredibly common.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,680
Up to 80% of women develop them by age 50, according to the NIH.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,120
A few everyday habits appear to raise that risk even further.

7
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:23,760
First, a diet heavy in red meat.

8
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:30,080
One study found women who ate the most red meat had about 1.7 times higher odds of fibroids.

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,840
Diets rich in green vegetables and fruit were linked to lower risk.

10
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,240
You don't have to cut red meat out completely.

11
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:39,840
Swapping in fish or legumes a couple of times a week may help.

12
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:42,320
Loading your plate with vegetables helps too.

13
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,720
Second, regular alcohol use.

14
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,720
Alcohol is linked to higher estrogen levels in premenopausal women.

15
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:53,040
Daily drinkers face notably higher fibroid risk than non-drinkers.

16
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,200
You don't need to quit drinking altogether.

17
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:58,560
Building in a few alcohol-free days each week may help.

18
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:01,600
Cutting back on how much you have in one sitting helps too.

19
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,680
Third, low vitamin D.

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,240
Women with sufficient vitamin D had about 32% lower odds of fibroids than those with a deficiency, an NIH-funded study found.

21
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:14,960
Getting some sunlight can help close that gap.

22
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:19,040
So can vitamin D-rich foods like salmon or eggs, or a supplement.

23
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:23,760
A Mediterranean-style diet is also linked to lower fibroid risk overall.

24
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:28,080
Fibroids also tend to show up earlier and more severely in Black women.

25
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,800
Don't brush off symptoms just because you're young.

26
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:35,280
If your periods are unusually heavy, an ultrasound can confirm what's going on.

27
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,080
Treatment options vary by size and location.

28
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:43,280
Cutting back on red meat and alcohol while adding more vitamin D is a simple place to start.
